 "scoring": "The form's scoring box records, for each domain and overall: Number of Items Scored '2' or '3'; Total Score; Mean Score (N/A items not included in calculation); and the number of answered questions the mean is calculated from. Higher scores indicate greater impairment. The form itself prints no cut offs. Weiss's scoring guidance, as summarised in the target record and the WFIRS literature, treats a domain mean of 1.5 or above, or 2 items scored 2 or 1 item scored 3 within a domain, as clinically significant impairment; this threshold is not printed on the UCC copy and should be verified against Weiss's published scoring instructions.",
 "citation": "Weiss, M. D. (2000). Weiss Functional Impairment Rating Scale – Self Report (WFIRS-S) [Measurement instrument]. University of British Columbia.",
 "transcriptionNote": "All 69 items transcribed from the UCC Student Health Service PDF, title 'WEISS FUNCTIONAL IMPAIRMENT RATING SCALE – SELF REPORT (WFIRS-S)'. Items are numbered 1 to 69 sequentially here; the source numbers items within each lettered domain (A1 to G14) and the source label is given in each item note. The form prints the 4 response labels plus n/a but does not print the numbers 0 to 3; the 0 to 3 values are inferred from the scoring box, which refers to items scored '2' or '3'. Spelling follows the form (behavioural, neighbours). WebFetch returned the items in 3 domain batches; the instruction and copyright statement were returned in consecutive fragments and rejoined."
